  "thread": "elaine: Heads-up \u2014 docs CI is failing on staging after the MDX migration. mkdocs linkcheck shows broken fragments that point into inline SVGs.\nci-bot: build failed (mkdocs-linkcheck) \u2014 4 broken links detected. See details in CI.\nelaine: Paste from the linkcheck log: \n```\nERROR    -  file:///workspace/site/guide/index.html: broken link: /docs/guide#svg-icons (fragment not found)\nERROR    -  file:///workspace/site/overview.html: broken link: /docs/overview#app-logo (fragment not found)\n```\n\nmike: Do those IDs exist in the source MDX?\n\nelaine: They do \u2014 we inline SVGs like \"<svg id=\\\"svg-icons\\\">\" inside examples. Locally the dev server scrolls fine, but linkcheck treats the svg fragment as missing.\n\njess: I think the MDX transformer is hoisting/rewriting the SVG and losing the id attribute during the code block -> rendered HTML pass. Also saw some examples where prettier mdx wrapping inserted a ZWSP before the `#` in headings inside code samples which messed with slug generation.\n\nmike: OK. Two paths: (A) teach linkcheck to ignore fragments that target inline SVGs, or (B) add explicit fallback anchors \"<a id=\\\"svg-icons\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"></a>\" before the svg. I prefer B as short-term.\n\nelaine: Short-term fallback SGTM. Long-term we should fix the MDX pipeline so IDs are stable. I can open a PR to add fallback anchors to affected docs pages.\n\njess: I'll also open a follow-up PR against the mdx preprocessor to preserve id attrs in inline SVGs \u2014 it's causing other subtle link / styling issues.\n\nmike: Who wants to own the CI config change? We should add a linkcheck ignore rule for svg fragments while we roll out fixes.\n\nelaine: I'll add the ignore rule in the linkcheck config in the PR so the staging build unblocks. PR plan: 1) docs content PR with \"<a id=...>\" fallbacks + linkcheck ignore, 2) mdx preprocessor PR to keep ids (code changes tracked), 3) cleanup pass to remove fallback anchors after preprocessor fix.\n\njess: Noted. I'll include a unit test for slug/id preservation in the mdx transformer.\n\nmike: Can you drop PR links here once they're up? I'll queue the staging redeploy after the linkcheck ignore lands. :eyes:\n\nelaine: PRs: docs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1832, mdx fix: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/762 \u2014 both opened. Added short description and screenshots in the PRs.\n\nci-bot: /retest queued for staging after docs PR merge.\n\nmike: Great. Assigning reviewers: @jess on infra PR, @mike on docs content. I'll follow up with QA to spot-check anchors on mobile. :shipit:\n\nelaine: Thanks \u2014 I'll remove the fallback anchors in a cleanup PR once the transformer change is merged.\n\njess: One more note \u2014 when you add the fallback anchors please use `aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"` and a short comment so future editors know why they're there.\n\nelaine: Yep will do. Closing loop here \u2014 will ping when staging is green. :thumbsup:\n\nmike: Thanks all!",
